# Upstream's root .gitignore has a blanket `bin/` rule (line 53) aimed at build
# output. It also swallowed worlddungeon/bin/ — so wd-migrate, wd-backup,
# wd-backup-nightly and wd-baseline were never version-controlled, despite F2/F3
# existing precisely so that custom tooling and data are reproducible. The
# nightly backup script that protects the database was itself unbacked-up.
#
# Re-include it here rather than editing the root file, per F2's rule that
# WorldDungeon stays outside upstream paths so an upstream merge can't conflict.
# A nested .gitignore takes precedence for paths beneath it, and the directory
# itself must be un-excluded before anything inside it can be re-included.
!bin/
!bin/*
